From: abdullahshoieb90-source
 <226442234+abdullahshoieb90-source@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:31:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hud): add Hotbar Slot module (ported from
 LeviLaunchroid)

Ported from LeviLaunchroid's inbuilt hotbar_slot module as an in-game
HUD row: nine 1-9 hotbar slot cells (per-slot show toggles, size, gap,
background/opacity, draggable HUD editor element). The "Use Item Icons"
mode mirrors the launcher's hollow-frame buttons: a cell holding an
item is drawn without its number as a translucent window so a vanilla
hotbar item stays visible underneath. Item presence uses the same
container-walk offsets as core/InventoryAccess.cpp.

A selected-slot highlight is intentionally left out until a
selected-slot signature is resolved (no guessed offsets, per project
policy); display-only by design because in-game slot selection is the
vanilla hotbar itself.
