+## Hotbar Slot
+
+Ported from the inbuilt **hotbar_slot** module of
+[LeviLaunchroid](https://github.com/LiteLDev/LeviLaunchroid) (its
+`HotbarSlotOverlay` + `InbuiltOverlayManager` row layout + `InbuiltModManager`
+settings).
+
+In LeviLauncher the feature is a launcher-side overlay: nine separate 1–9
+buttons above the game for selecting hotbar slots, each individually hideable,
+with an *item icons* mode that hollows a button out so the vanilla hotbar item
+shows through. Inside the game (this repo) it becomes an on-screen HUD row of
+the same nine slots:
+
+- Default number labels on each cell (1–9), like the launcher buttons.
+- **Use Item Icons** mode: a cell that currently holds an item is drawn as a
+  translucent window without its number, so a vanilla hotbar item placed under
+  it stays visible (mirrors the hollow-frame mode of the launcher).
+- Per-slot show toggles (chips group "Show Slots"), slot size, gap, background
+  and opacity controls, and a draggable HUD-editor element; default placement
+  auto-centres the row just above the vanilla hotbar.
+
+Known port notes:
+
+- Item presence per slot is read with the same container-walk offsets as
+  `src/core/InventoryAccess.cpp` (hotbar = container indices 0–8).
+- A "currently selected slot" highlight is intentionally not included: it needs
+  a selected-slot signature/offset that has not been resolved in this codebase,
+  and offsets are never guessed here (see the `MinecraftLoader`-style policy).
+  Once such a signature is added, highlighting the active cell is a small
+  addition in `onFrame()`.
+- The original module also *selected* the slot when a button was pressed. In a
+  native in-game mod that action is simply the vanilla hotbar itself, so the
+  HUD is display-only by design.
+
